            <header class="lesson-header"><span class="lesson-number">Lesson 9</span><h1>Change Tracking</h1><div class="lesson-meta"><span class="lesson-duration"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>25 min</span><span class="lesson-level intermediate">Intermediate</span></div></header>
            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Entity States</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Detached - Not tracked by the context
var product = new Product { Name = "Widget" };

// Added - Will be inserted
context.Products.Add(product);  // State = Added

// Unchanged - Loaded from DB, no changes
var loaded = await context.Products.FindAsync(1);  // State = Unchanged

// Modified - Tracked entity with changes
loaded.Price = 99.99m;  // State = Modified

// Deleted - Will be deleted
context.Products.Remove(loaded);  // State = Deleted</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Checking Entity State</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">var entry = context.Entry(product);
Console.WriteLine(entry.State);  // EntityState enum

// Check modified properties
if (entry.State == EntityState.Modified)
{
    foreach (var prop in entry.Properties)
    {
        if (prop.IsModified)
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"{prop.Metadata.Name}: {prop.OriginalValue} -> {prop.CurrentValue}");
        }
    }
}</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>No-Tracking Queries</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Read-only queries (better performance)
var products = await context.Products
    .AsNoTracking()
    .ToListAsync();

// Changes won't be detected
products[0].Price = 0;  // Won't be saved!

// Configure globally for read-heavy scenarios
context.ChangeTracker.QueryTrackingBehavior = QueryTrackingBehavior.NoTracking;

// Or in DbContext
protected override void OnConfiguring(DbContextOptionsBuilder options)
{
    options.UseQueryTrackingBehavior(QueryTrackingBehavior.NoTracking);
}</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Attaching Entities</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Attach disconnected entity (State = Unchanged)
context.Products.Attach(product);

// Attach as modified (will update all properties)
context.Products.Update(product);

// Attach and mark specific properties modified
context.Products.Attach(product);
context.Entry(product).Property(p => p.Price).IsModified = true;</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>ChangeTracker Debugging</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// View all tracked entities
Console.WriteLine(context.ChangeTracker.DebugView.LongView);

// Count tracked entities
var tracked = context.ChangeTracker.Entries().Count();

// Get pending changes
var added = context.ChangeTracker.Entries()
    .Where(e => e.State == EntityState.Added)
    .ToList();</code></pre>
                </section>

                <LessonTakeaways>
                    <LessonTakeaway>EF Core tracks entity states: Added, Modified, Deleted, Unchanged.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Use AsNoTracking() for read-only queries.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Attach/Update for disconnected scenarios.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>DebugView helps troubleshoot tracking issues.</LessonTakeaway>
                </LessonTakeaways>
